{{!
    @template enrol_apply/review_actions

    The three decisions, rendered into a core sticky footer by the renderer.

    Only the decisions live here: a core sticky footer is a fixed box, 80px at default font
    sizes, whose content area clips with no scrollbar, so the message box and the two choosers
    stay in the page body, as on the queue.

    Each button carries name formaction and its own value, so the button pressed is the decision
    taken and manage.php reads it with optional_param. It must stay a named form control: the
    HTML5 formaction attribute would post nothing under that name.

    The destructive decision comes first in source order and is pushed to the far edge by this
    row's own justify-content-between. The footer's classes apply to a content area whose only
    child is this row, so they have nothing to spread.

    Being first also makes Cancel the form's default submit, which is what Enter in a chooser
    triggers. That is safe only because manage.php intercepts formaction cancel from the review
    page and asks for confirmation; whichever button comes first becomes the default, so no order
    makes both safe. Reordering these buttons without moving that interception would let Enter
    in a chooser enrol the applicant silently.

    The row does not wrap, because a wrapped second line would be clipped out of sight; below
    the width the three labels need, it scrolls sideways instead (styles.css).

    Context variables required for this template:
    * actions array - one entry per decision, each with:
      * value string - what travels as formaction
      * label string - the button's text
      * style string - the Bootstrap button class it carries

    Example context (json):
    {
        "actions": [
            {"value": "cancel", "label": "Cancel this application", "style": "btn-outline-danger"},
            {"value": "wait", "label": "Defer this application", "style": "btn-secondary"},
            {"value": "confirm", "label": "Confirm this application", "style": "btn-primary"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-reviewactions d-flex flex-nowrap justify-content-between align-items-center gap-2 w-100">
    {{#actions}}
        <button type="submit" name="formaction" value="{{value}}" class="btn {{style}}">
            {{label}}
        </button>
    {{/actions}}
</div>
